{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "1CO",
  "chapter": 13,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.13.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though I speak with the tongues of men and of angels, and have not charity, I am become ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sounding brass, or a tinkling cymbal.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.13.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And though I have ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the gift of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " prophecy, and understand all mysteries, and all knowledge; and though I have all faith, so that I could remove mountains, and have not charity, I am nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.13.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And though I bestow all my goods to feed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the poor",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and though I give my body to be burned, and have not charity, it profiteth me nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.13.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Charity suffereth long, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is kind; charity envieth not; charity vaunteth not itself, is not puffed up,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.13.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Doth not behave itself unseemly, seeketh not its own, is not easily provoked, thinketh no evil;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.13.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Rejoiceth not in iniquity, but rejoiceth in the truth;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.13.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Beareth all things, believeth all things, hopeth all things, endureth all things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.13.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Charity never faileth: but whether ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " prophecies, they shall fail; whether ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " languages, they shall cease; whether ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " knowledge, it shall vanish away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.13.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we know in part, and we prophesy in part.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.13.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But when that which is perfect is come, then that which is in part shall be done away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.13.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I was a child, I spoke as a child, I understood as a child, I thought as a child: but when I became a man, I put away childish things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.13.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For now we see through a glass darkly; but then face to face: now I know in part; but then shall I know even as also I am known.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CO.13.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now abideth faith, hope, charity, these three; but the greatest of these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " charity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
